{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E78mjtERyrnVCvaFCwdNer","type":"tool_result","content":"appended skill2\n     343 /tmp/claude_build/build.py","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9069a765-b3ee-4a03-8f71-6288ce3b57b6","uuid":"b6fea534-9483-4017-8198-372c0000a8ad","timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:34:09.847Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"appended skill2\n     343 /tmp/claude_build/build.py","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01E78mjtERyrnVCvaFCwdNer","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CgNB3ykWfT1wRxjtrktHG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012DujimcYzxyhJgowta9q34","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /tmp/claude_build/build.py <<'PYEOF'\nART[\"build_tenants/claude/skills/stdo-delegate-review/SKILL.md\"] = r'''---\nname: stdo-delegate-review\ndescription: Use when governed STDO work in this repository needs a bounded worker handoff or a required independent review — preserving the governing requirement, design, grant, territory, proof predicates, and return across the handoff, and deriving review expectations from sources before judging a candidate. Not for unrelated tasks.\n---\n\n# STDO delegation and independent review\n\nUse this skill when the triage in `stdo-workspace-change` shows that the work\ngenuinely needs a separate worker, a separate reviewer, or both.\n\n## Delegating a bounded worker (SK-06, Q05)\n\nWhen you delegate construction (direct or to another actor), the worker must\nreceive: the governing requirement and design, the exact operation grant and\nterritory, the applicable proof predicates, and a bounded return definition.\n\n- Preserve these bindings across the actual host handoff; a child does not\n  inherit your whole context merely because it is available.\n- A child completion does **not** start an unrequested next stage. The Executive\n  consumes the child's closed return and then selects the next authorized action.\n- Keep these distinct in the record: actor output, transport success, candidate\n  availability, assessment, and acceptance. One does not imply the next.\n\nA worker returns the exact candidate, the performed and the not-performed\nevaluations, the effects, the residuals, and the invalidators — not a fluent\nsummary.\n\n## Independent review (SK-07, Q05, Q09)\n\nWhen a change requires independent review:\n\n1. The reviewer derives expected behavior from the governing sources **before**\n   seeing the candidate's own claims.\n2. The reviewer then evaluates the exact frozen candidate and its actual-path\n   proof.\n3. The reviewer reports actual exposure, evidence, severity, and affected claims.\n   It does **not** author the adopted repair and does **not** assume acceptance\n   authority. A different role label alone does not establish independence.\n\nA required fresh assessment after a material change cannot be replaced by a stale\nreview result (see `stdo-continuation` for invalidation).\n\n## Same-model-family limit\n\nA non-author reviewer in the same model family supplies non-author evidence with\na semantic-independence limitation; it does not establish cross-family\nindependence. State this limit when it applies.\n\n## Method sources (cited, not reproduced)\n\nWithin `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/`: `EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md` sections\n6, 8 to 10, 12, and 16 to 19 for role configuration and bounded Executive\ndecisions; `EVALUATION.md` sections 3, 5, and 7 for independent review and\nacceptance; `ASSURANCE.md` sections 7 to 9 for actual-path proof.\n\n## Scope and limits\n\nThis skill coordinates roles; it does not itself grant effect authority or decide\nacceptance. Acceptance and release remain the owner's decisions.\n'''\nPYEOF\necho appended skill3; wc -l /tmp/claude_build/build.py","description":"Append stdo-delegate-review skill"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1843,"cache_read_input_tokens":197997,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1843},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9069a765-b3ee-4a03-8f71-6288ce3b57b6","uuid":"ac38d49e-37e7-4636-a854-b73e46ecad45","timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:34:24.902Z","request_id":"req_011CgNB3yNCB5WGCsMFG2mW3","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012DujimcYzxyhJgowta9q34":{"command":"cat >> /tmp/claude_build/build.py <<'PYEOF'\nART[\"build_tenants/claude/skills/stdo-delegate-review/SKILL.md\"] = r'''---\nname: stdo-delegate-review\ndescription: Use when governed STDO work in this repository needs a bounded worker handoff or a required independent review — preserving the governing requirement, design, grant, territory, proof predicates, and return across the handoff, and deriving review expectations from sources before judging a candidate. Not for unrelated tasks.\n---\n\n# STDO delegation and independent review\n\nUse this skill when the triage in `stdo-workspace-change` shows that the work\ngenuinely needs a separate worker, a separate reviewer, or both.\n\n## Delegating a bounded worker (SK-06, Q05)\n\nWhen you delegate construction (direct or to another actor), the worker must\nreceive: the governing requirement and design, the exact operation grant and\nterritory, the applicable proof predicates, and a bounded return definition.\n\n- Preserve these bindings across the actual host handoff; a child does not\n  inherit your whole context merely because it is available.\n- A child completion does **not** start an unrequested next stage. The Executive\n  consumes the child's closed return and then selects the next authorized action.\n- Keep these distinct in the record: actor output, transport success, candidate\n  availability, assessment, and acceptance. One does not imply the next.\n\nA worker returns the exact candidate, the performed and the not-performed\nevaluations, the effects, the residuals, and the invalidators — not a fluent\nsummary.\n\n## Independent review (SK-07, Q05, Q09)\n\nWhen a change requires independent review:\n\n1. The reviewer derives expected behavior from the governing sources **before**\n   seeing the candidate's own claims.\n2. The reviewer then evaluates the exact frozen candidate and its actual-path\n   proof.\n3. The reviewer reports actual exposure, evidence, severity, and affected claims.\n   It does **not** author the adopted repair and does **not** assume acceptance\n   authority. A different role label alone does not establish independence.\n\nA required fresh assessment after a material change cannot be replaced by a stale\nreview result (see `stdo-continuation` for invalidation).\n\n## Same-model-family limit\n\nA non-author reviewer in the same model family supplies non-author evidence with\na semantic-independence limitation; it does not establish cross-family\nindependence. State this limit when it applies.\n\n## Method sources (cited, not reproduced)\n\nWithin `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/`: `EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md` sections\n6, 8 to 10, 12, and 16 to 19 for role configuration and bounded Executive\ndecisions; `EVALUATION.md` sections 3, 5, and 7 for independent review and\nacceptance; `ASSURANCE.md` sections 7 to 9 for actual-path proof.\n\n## Scope and limits\n\nThis skill coordinates roles; it does not itself grant effect authority or decide\nacceptance. Acceptance and release remain the owner's decisions.\n'''\nPYEOF\necho appended skill3; wc -l /tmp/claude_build/build.py","description":"Append stdo-delegate-review skill"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012DujimcYzxyhJgowta9q34","type":"tool_result","content":"appended skill3\n     403 /tmp/claude_build/build.py","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9069a765-b3ee-4a03-8f71-6288ce3b57b6","uuid":"e5deb92b-2fa0-485e-8658-56cdc2d764b1","timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:34:24.931Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"appended skill3\n     403 /tmp/claude_build/build.py","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012DujimcYzxyhJgowta9q34","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CgNB56GwvyyYE9UKMSbum","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Dvi9eFeuDq22G4DtGdFXji","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /tmp/claude_build/build.py <<'PYEOF'\nART[\"build_tenants/claude/skills/stdo-continuation/SKILL.md\"] = r'''---\nname: stdo-continuation\ndescription: Use when resuming interrupted or prior governed STDO work in this repository, reconciling observed effects before retry, reporting truthful status and closure, or capturing qualification evidence. Keeps candidate availability, indeterminate assessment, and not-performed distinct. Not for unrelated tasks.\n---\n\n# STDO continuation, status, and evidence\n\nUse this skill on resume, after an interruption, when writing status, or when\nrecording evidence for qualification.\n\n## Resume and reconcile (SK-08, Q07, Q08)\n\nOn resume or after an interrupted effect:\n\n1. Acquire the material current state (re-observe the targets and read the\n   retained records) before any retry.\n2. Reconcile observed effects: if a target already changed, do not repeat the\n   effect; a timeout does not prove rollback, and a repeated request must not\n   duplicate an uncertain effect.\n3. Retain unresolved obligations and still-valid evidence; invalidate only the\n   reliance actually affected, each with its reason.\n\nTwo histories with identical candidate bytes are not interchangeable: one may\ncarry a current accepted assessment and another an unresolved counterexample that\ninvalidates its assessment. The retained obligation cannot disappear into a\ncandidate-only summary — the continuations differ (Q07).\n\n## Status and closure (SK-09, Q09, Q10)\n\nState what was actually constructed, assessed, and decided: the exact subject,\nthe basis, the evidence, and the remaining work.\n\n- Distinguish, with the correct predicate, the three outcomes: an exact\n  **candidate is available**; an assessment was **performed but indeterminate**;\n  an assessment was **not performed** (no result) and remains a residual. Never\n  collapse these into one \"done\" or one \"exhausted\" verdict (Q10).\n- Closure follows the applicable predicates and required dispositions — not a\n  test count, not the mere occurrence of a review, not a fluent summary.\n- An unsupported or unperformed case stays visible; it is never reported as a\n  passing result.\n- When a governed source or candidate materially changes, withdraw the affected\n  reliance (including a prior passing review) and keep the missing reassessment\n  open; unrelated valid observations remain reusable (Q09).\n\n## Capture evidence (SK-12, Q01, Q12)\n\nFor any qualification trial, retain the actual invocation, the acquired inputs,\nthe outputs, the tool traces, the observed effects, the elapsed time, and any\nreported token or cost data. Measures that are unavailable stay **unknown** — do\nnot invent them. Compare equivalent substantive information, and count retries,\nrepair, and review in the total cost. One passing trial is bounded evidence for\nthe exact case, host, and settings observed; it is not a success rate or a\ngeneral benefit claim. A keyword or formatting check may establish structure but\nnot successful method application.\n\n## Method sources (cited, not reproduced)\n\nWithin `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/`: `ACTIVATION.md` sections 5 and 7\nand `FOUNDATIONS.md` (observation sufficiency) for restart, retained results, and\ninvalidation; `ACTIVATION.md` section 3 for result and disposition;\n`EVALUATION.md` section 7 and `ASSURANCE.md` sections 7 to 9 for test semantics\nand actual-path proof.\n\n## Scope and limits\n\nThis skill records and reconciles; it does not itself qualify host behavior or\ngrant acceptance.\n'''\nPYEOF\necho appended skill4; wc -l /tmp/claude_build/build.py","description":"Append stdo-continuation skill"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1179,"cache_read_input_tokens":199840,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1179},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9069a765-b3ee-4a03-8f71-6288ce3b57b6","uuid":"224e1a20-f574-4020-be07-046e2463a107","timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:34:41.708Z","request_id":"req_011CgNB55se3FpfCqM8nvb7j","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Dvi9eFeuDq22G4DtGdFXji":{"command":"cat >> /tmp/claude_build/build.py <<'PYEOF'\nART[\"build_tenants/claude/skills/stdo-continuation/SKILL.md\"] = r'''---\nname: stdo-continuation\ndescription: Use when resuming interrupted or prior governed STDO work in this repository, reconciling observed effects before retry, reporting truthful status and closure, or capturing qualification evidence. Keeps candidate availability, indeterminate assessment, and not-performed distinct. Not for unrelated tasks.\n---\n\n# STDO continuation, status, and evidence\n\nUse this skill on resume, after an interruption, when writing status, or when\nrecording evidence for qualification.\n\n## Resume and reconcile (SK-08, Q07, Q08)\n\nOn resume or after an interrupted effect:\n\n1. Acquire the material current state (re-observe the targets and read the\n   retained records) before any retry.\n2. Reconcile observed effects: if a target already changed, do not repeat the\n   effect; a timeout does not prove rollback, and a repeated request must not\n   duplicate an uncertain effect.\n3. Retain unresolved obligations and still-valid evidence; invalidate only the\n   reliance actually affected, each with its reason.\n\nTwo histories with identical candidate bytes are not interchangeable: one may\ncarry a current accepted assessment and another an unresolved counterexample that\ninvalidates its assessment. The retained obligation cannot disappear into a\ncandidate-only summary — the continuations differ (Q07).\n\n## Status and closure (SK-09, Q09, Q10)\n\nState what was actually constructed, assessed, and decided: the exact subject,\nthe basis, the evidence, and the remaining work.\n\n- Distinguish, with the correct predicate, the three outcomes: an exact\n  **candidate is available**; an assessment was **performed but indeterminate**;\n  an assessment was **not performed** (no result) and remains a residual. Never\n  collapse these into one \"done\" or one \"exhausted\" verdict (Q10).\n- Closure follows the applicable predicates and required dispositions — not a\n  test count, not the mere occurrence of a review, not a fluent summary.\n- An unsupported or unperformed case stays visible; it is never reported as a\n  passing result.\n- When a governed source or candidate materially changes, withdraw the affected\n  reliance (including a prior passing review) and keep the missing reassessment\n  open; unrelated valid observations remain reusable (Q09).\n\n## Capture evidence (SK-12, Q01, Q12)\n\nFor any qualification trial, retain the actual invocation, the acquired inputs,\nthe outputs, the tool traces, the observed effects, the elapsed time, and any\nreported token or cost data. Measures that are unavailable stay **unknown** — do\nnot invent them. Compare equivalent substantive information, and count retries,\nrepair, and review in the total cost. One passing trial is bounded evidence for\nthe exact case, host, and settings observed; it is not a success rate or a\ngeneral benefit claim. A keyword or formatting check may establish structure but\nnot successful method application.\n\n## Method sources (cited, not reproduced)\n\nWithin `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/`: `ACTIVATION.md` sections 5 and 7\nand `FOUNDATIONS.md` (observation sufficiency) for restart, retained results, and\ninvalidation; `ACTIVATION.md` section 3 for result and disposition;\n`EVALUATION.md` section 7 and `ASSURANCE.md` sections 7 to 9 for test semantics\nand actual-path proof.\n\n## Scope and limits\n\nThis skill records and reconciles; it does not itself qualify host behavior or\ngrant acceptance.\n'''\nPYEOF\necho appended skill4; wc -l /tmp/claude_build/build.py","description":"Append stdo-continuation skill"}}}
